# Git Commits — User Only Unless Explicitly Directed

**DO NOT commit without the user's explicit direction.**

- Only create git commits when the user explicitly asks (e.g. "commit this", "create a commit").
- If unclear, ask first — never assume.
- Requests for a commit **message** (e.g. "commit msg", "suggested commit message") mean provide the message only; the user commits.
- Do not stage or commit proactively after fixing code, tests, or lint issues.
- Do not push unless explicitly asked.
